 The vector path preserves scalar face order for equal-time hits, handles
 parallel faces without dividing by zero, and uses the scalar loop for the
-remaining one to three faces. It adds no geometry allocation or RDMA metadata.
+remaining one to three faces. CPU builds also keep contiguous normal components
+for SIMD loads (24 extra bytes per directed face), rebuilt with the existing
+geometry snapshot after mesh changes. Host transport views are invalidated each
+step before taking pointers into that snapshot. Random-walk radius selection
+uses the same SIMD geometry, and leak-time interpolation caches logarithms of
+the actual stored tau values. No RDMA descriptor or particle wire layout changes.
 Stationary-frame IMC events also reuse their identical attenuation exponential;
 moving-frame events retain separate factors when the Doppler shift differs
 from one.
